# Global rules — Haque Consultancy site

You are working on a **professional consulting website**, not a portfolio,
not a tech demo. When in doubt, choose simpler over flashier and slower.

## Always

- Read `design.mdc` and `tech.mdc` before making structural changes.
- Default to existing components (`Button`, `SectionTitle`, `ServiceCard`,
  `card` / `card-soft` classes) before writing new ones.
- Run `npm run lint` and `npm run build` after non-trivial changes.
  Both must succeed with **zero warnings**.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`. The global stylesheet already zeroes
  out animations under that media query; do not bypass it.
- Maintain accessibility: every interactive element must be reachable via
  keyboard, have a visible focus ring, and carry an accurate
  `aria-label` if the visible text is missing.
- Use semantic HTML: `<header>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<section>`,
  `<article>`, `<footer>`. Avoid `<div>` soup.

## Never

- Introduce neon colors, cyan/purple gradients, or glowing hover effects.
- Add particle backgrounds, WebGL canvases, custom cursors, parallax,
  or letter-by-letter stagger animations.
- Add carousels, sliders, marquees, or auto-playing media.
- Use emojis as icons (use `lucide-react`).
- Add a third-party font via `<link>` — use `next/font` exclusively.
- Add a dependency without checking the bundle impact (see budget in
  `tech.mdc`).
- Commit `.next/`, `out/`, or any generated artifact.
- Push to `main` without confirming the GitHub Actions deploy succeeded.

## Content tone

- Plain, confident, specific. No buzzwords ("synergy", "leverage", "cutting-edge").
- Outcomes over features. Every service description ends in a tangible result.
- No vague stats. If we can't back a number up, we don't print it.
- Write in second person ("you / your business"), present tense.

## When the user asks for "a redesign" or "more flashy"

- Push back politely. The brand identity is intentionally calm. Suggest a
  small, restrained alternative (e.g. one more accent moment, an extra
  whitespace pass) instead of reintroducing forbidden patterns.

## Editing checklist before "done"

- [ ] No console errors on load (DevTools → Console).
- [ ] No CLS shifts when images / fonts load.
- [ ] Looks correct at 320 px, 768 px, 1024 px, 1440 px.
- [ ] `Tab` key navigates the whole page in logical order.
- [ ] `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` disables non-essential animation.
- [ ] Lighthouse mobile performance ≥ 90.
